Create a new standard-library-only TypeScript module exporting the following numeric API:

```ts
export interface Point { readonly x: number; readonly y: number; }
export function wrapHalfOpen(value: number, lower: number, upper: number): number;
export function bound(value: number, lower: number, upper: number): number;
export function blend(from: number, to: number, fraction: number): number;
export function cubicPoint(a: Point, b: Point, c: Point, d: Point, fraction: number): Point;
export function smoothStep(fraction: number): number;
export function selectOwn<T extends object, K extends keyof T>(source: T, keys: readonly K[]): Pick<T, K>;
```

Every numeric argument must be finite or the function must throw `RangeError`. Bounds require `lower < upper`. `wrapHalfOpen` maps values of any magnitude into `[lower, upper)`. `bound` returns the nearest value in the closed interval `[lower, upper]`. `blend` and `cubicPoint` require a fraction in `[0,1]` and do not mutate points. `smoothStep` also requires `[0,1]` and computes `3t² - 2t³`. `selectOwn` copies only requested own properties that actually exist, ignores inherited and missing properties, processes duplicate keys once, preserves key-request order, and returns a new object. It must not mutate or alias the source object itself; property values may remain shallow references.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

